From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:50:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: don't ask for compressed textures

The game uploads its textures as GL_COMPRESSED_RGBA_ARB when the
extension is there. OSMesa's software rasteriser then stores them as DXT3
and decodes a 4x4 block for every texel it samples: a profile of CAM_1A at
800x600 spent 44% of the time in fetch_rgba_dxt3/fetch_compressed.
Uploading plain GL_RGBA doubles the frame rate (11 -> 21 fps on the
profiling host) for about 10MB more memory, and looks better, since DXT is
lossy.
---
 lib/ivis_opengl/piemode.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/ivis_opengl/piemode.c b/lib/ivis_opengl/piemode.c
index 6e89038..318e277 100644
--- a/lib/ivis_opengl/piemode.c
+++ b/lib/ivis_opengl/piemode.c
@@ -56,8 +56,14 @@ BOOL pie_Initialise(void)
 	rendSurface.buffer = NULL;
 	rendSurface.size = 0;
 
-	/* Find texture compression extension */
+	/* Find texture compression extension. Not on RISC OS: software OpenGL
+	 * would store the textures compressed and decode a block for every
+	 * texel it samples, which halves the frame rate. */
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+	if (false)
+#else
 	if (GLEE_ARB_texture_compression)
+#endif
 	{
 		debug(LOG_TEXTURE, "Texture compression: Yes");
 		wz_texture_compression = GL_COMPRESSED_RGBA_ARB;
